## Lore

Slurmphs, the "Slug Men", are rotund, slug-like D-Bees found toiling on farms
and orchards across rural North America, hauling garbage and catching pests in
the cities, or laughing over drinks in a tavern. They stand on two
tree-trunk legs, with oven-mitt hands, pale grey or white skin blotched with
brown, no eyes or ears, and a vertical slit of a mouth that gapes wide to
swallow food whole and leaves it to dissolve into a foul paste. Everything they
touch ends up coated in their slime, and most people find them revolting.

Despite the looks and the smell they are easygoing, friendly and generous,
always willing to lend a hand, and usually happy even when drunk, which happens
fast, on as little as two beers. They will eat almost anything, rotting
garbage and roadkill included.

They are superb farmers with an uncanny feel for growing things, and many turn
their harvests into wines and liquors sold at markets and occasionally on the
Black Market. Now and then wanderlust takes one, often in search of a new
flavor, and some become explorers, adventurers, mercenaries or scholars.

## GM Notes

Pronounced "slur muff". Also known as Slug Men and Slime Balls. Size 6-7 feet
(1.8 to 2.1 m). Weight 170-350 pounds (77 to 158 kg). Life span 2D6+62 years.
Hermaphrodites who change gender to mate, roughly every three years; 2D4 tiny
live young after three months, abandoned to burrow underground for 2D6 months
and reach maturity within 1D4+3 years.

Habitat: anywhere in North America, most commonly the old Midwest, the Ohio
River Valley, the Great Lakes region and Mexico; the CS has driven them out of
southern Wisconsin, Iowa, Missouri and Arkansas. Slave market value 3D4x1,000
as farmers, 1D4x1,000 as labor or waste management; sometimes found in traveling
shows. Allies: often found with Idie Swamp Men, Larmac and occasionally a Butter
Troll. Enemies: the Coalition Army has slaughtered hundreds of thousands of them
over the last 35 years; Slurmphs hate and fear the CS.
